# Request budgets (soft-nav critical path)

Budgets make snappiness measurable and force lean builds. Do **not** invent a
Redis full-page cache to “meet” a budget (`framework-cache-contracts.mdc`,
`framework-components.mdc`).

## Critical path

| Class | Routes |
| --- | --- |
| `pages` | `GET /api/pages/...` |
| `navigation` | `GET /api/navigation/...` |
| `list_refresh` | Addon list endpoints used as live refresh |
| `other` | Default floors |

Diagnose pages and navigation separately before blaming Vite/HMR
(`framework-gui-live-updates.mdc`).

## Explicit ceilings

Source: `framework/runtimes/api/app/request_budgets.py` (`BUDGET_WARN` /
`BUDGET_FAIL`).

| Class | Warn (ms / sql / bytes) | Fail / defect (ms / sql / bytes) |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `pages` | 500 / 80 / 150 KiB | 2000 / 200 / 500 KiB |
| `navigation` | 300 / 60 / 50 KiB | 1000 / 100 / 150 KiB |
| `list_refresh` | 500 / 100 / 200 KiB | 2000 / 250 / 1 MiB |
| `other` | 500 / 200 / 100 KiB | 2000 / 400 / 500 KiB |

- **Warn:** logs `budget_miss=true` at WARNING — investigate.
- **Fail:** new work at or above these ceilings is a **defect**. Prefer
  batching and lean tiles over caching full page JSON.

## Observability

`framework.request` completion lines must expose `path`, `route`,
`duration_ms`, `sql_queries`, `response_bytes`, `critical_path`,
`budget_miss`, `budget_fail`, `budget_missed`. Never log secrets.
`Server-Timing` includes `app;dur=…` and an `sql` descriptor. GUI soft-nav
records `framework:navigation-*` measures and `console.debug`s total duration.

## Tests and hygiene

- Pin representative paths with `assert_sql_within_budget(...)`.
- Unbounded / obvious N+1 regressions must fail owner tests loudly.
- No definition-sync on hot authz/audit/settings reads; no per-row fat
  serializers when a request-scoped prefetch exists.
